      "writtenOn": "2025-03-10T18:50:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e RpcServerConnection has the flag: #[cfg(target_os \u003d \"trusty\")]. So this is specific to Trusty.\n\nThat\u0027s not a license to do anything you want, esp since you are depending on libbinder internals\n\n\u003e We need to reference this connection type\n\nBut why? \"we need to use it because we are using it\" isn\u0027t a reason",
      "parentUuid": "788a7a95_e85644bc",
      "revId": "b3b0e3333652e94541251ca9a5db8e99fdcf750b",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "923c147a_03f95a5f",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1678423
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-03-10T23:13:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e But why?\n\nLet me try to explain in a bit more detail, with reference to the tipc-userspace library.\n\n1. The `HandleSetWrapper` takes a generic parameter  - which is any concrete type (S) implementing the `UnbufferedService` trait. (https://android-review.git.corp.google.com/c/trusty/lib/+/3395648/28/lib/tipc/rust/src/raw/handle_set_wrapper.rs#30)\n\n\n2. `ServiceHandle` uses in its fields: `S` as the service and `S::Connection` (the associated type of `UnbufferedService` trait) in the `HandleType` enum. (https://android-review.git.corp.google.com/c/trusty/lib/+/3395648/35/lib/tipc/rust/src/raw/service_handle.rs#26)\n\n(We could not pass in a dyn of `UnbufferedService` instead of the aforementioned generic parameter because of the issues with flat pointers)\n\n3. In AuthMgr BE TA, we have two different concrete types implementing `UnbufferedService` trait that need to be served by the aforementioned `HandeSetWrapper`: `AuthMgrService` and `RpcServer`. https://android-review.git.corp.google.com/c/trusty/app/authmgr/+/3525490/12/authmgr-be/lib/src/server.rs#210\n\n\n4. I do not know any other way to address the requirement in #4 above, without referencig `RpcServerConnection` in the implementation of the service/connection multiplexing mechanism here: https://android-review.git.corp.google.com/c/trusty/app/authmgr/+/3525490/12/authmgr-be/lib/src/server.rs#216\n\nI am open to any suggestions for alternative ways of achieving the above requrement without having to export `RpcServerConnection`, if there is any. Please let me know your thoughts. Thanks!",
      "parentUuid": "d4c3e649_cb5073b1",
      "revId": "b3b0e3333652e94541251ca9a5db8e99fdcf750b",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
